Subject: Scryfall: default to a released paper printing, honour finishes

A line that names no set used Scryfall's default printing, which is its
newest: on 2026-10-11 "Swamp" was Marvel: Darkhold Destiny #296, a preview
released 2027-04-09 with games: [] and no prices, so scryfall_price_list
listed it as "no price" and format_archidekt with include_set_codes wrote
"(mdd) 296". format_archidekt also put *F* on whatever printing came back:
"1x Sol Ring (frc) 21 *F*", but FRC #21 only exists nonfoil. And in
scryfall_price_list a pinned line ("2x Sol Ring (ltc) 284") answered for an
unpinned line of the same card ("1 Sol Ring"), because both shared one
/cards/collection request and the result index is first-card-wins by name.

This patch:
- picks, for lines that name no set, the newest printing released by today
  (UTC) that is sold on paper, in the line's finish when a printing has it
  (one oracleid search, only when Scryfall's default is no good);
- format_archidekt: the printing named with include_set_codes comes in the
  finish asked for; when no printing of the card has that finish, the line
  gets no marker and a warning naming the finishes it does come in (also
  without include_set_codes);
- scryfall_price_list: asks about name-only lines in requests of their own,
  so a pinned line of the same card cannot stand in;
- scryfall_price: when a finish filter finds nothing but the printing exists,
  says "LTC #284 exists, but not in foil: it only comes nonfoil" with the
  printing's details, instead of "No results found".
Tests: tests/test_default_printing.py.

Upstream: Kautiontape/mystic-forge at dd82cd1 (main, 2026-10-04) has no fix,
and no open pull request touches this code. Drop this patch when it does.

